 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Of course. Is it more important to start with the pasta sauces or the bread? Start by checking whether the sauces already contain gluten. Then look at the bread. A lot of shop bought crusty breads are fine. The simple ones usually are. Bread, pasta, rice, lentils, fruit, vegetables, eggs, meat and cheese. Soy sauce is often fine, but check the label. Some mix in flour. It is a big relief. Gluten free shopping gets easier with time. That's a common worry, but with careful labels, it doesn't have to happen.",
